## Acceptance: embedded release binary launches without network

`LTS_DATA_DIR=<tmp> LTS_SMOKE_FILE=<marker> xvfb-run -a ... ./target/release/lts-desktop`
with port 1420 verified FREE before launch. exit=0 and
`release-embedded-launch-marker.txt` shows: `smoke-ok home-rendered`,
13 `smoke-ok route:` acks, `goal-map-assert 77`, `smoke-ok routes-complete:5`.
The UI served from the embedded `frontendDist` — no dev server existed.

Harness incident (documented, not a product defect): the FIRST spot-check
attempt produced an empty marker because the single-instance plugin refused the
probe while the owner's PRE-FIX `target/release/lts-desktop` dogfood instance
(PID 913088, showing the reported connection-error screen) was still open.
That stale pre-fix instance was closed; the re-run passed as above. Also note:
headless launches on this box need `source scripts/tauri-env.sh` (user-local
webkit2gtk sysroot) — the first unit version missed it; the smoke/preview
scripts already source it.

